<div class="text">
<p>None of these credits means that the source endorses Traces Blanches. Trail maps drawn by ski resorts are never reused.</p>

<h2 id="maps">Maps on this site</h2>
<p>The maps on this site come from packs of several massifs (Hautes-Alpes, Vosges, Ariège Pyrenees, Haut-Jura) and from the census of Nordic ski areas. Each caption carries a short credit; here are the full sources.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Base map</b>: IGN, Plan IGN v2, Licence Ouverte 2.0.</li>
<li><b>Slopes and terrain</b>: IGN, LiDAR HD terrain model, Licence Ouverte 2.0.</li>
<li><b>Trails</b>: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0, daily OpenSnowMap extract; Nordic centres: Protomaps © OpenStreetMap contributors.</li>
<li><b>Grande Traversée du Jura</b>: route from <a href={link('datatourisme', 'en')} rel="noopener">DATAtourisme</a>, Licence Ouverte 2.0, and © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0; nearby routes from Camptocamp contributors, CC BY-SA 3.0.</li>
<li><b>Huts</b>: © refuges.info contributors, CC BY-SA.</li>
<li><b>No-signal areas</b>: ARCEP, Mon Réseau Mobile, maps of 30 June 2026, Licence Ouverte.</li>
<li><b>Map of France</b>: Nordic ski areas © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0, OpenSkiMap; Nordic backcountry areas from OpenStreetMap, <a href={link('geotrek', 'en')} rel="noopener">Geotrek</a> and DATAtourisme; packs built: project catalogue of 15 November 2026; department outlines: IGN Admin Express via Etalab, Licence Ouverte.</li>
</ul>
<p>No map on this site shows a source whose licence forbids sharing it.</p>

<h2 id="code">The code of the app</h2>
<p>The code of the app is open. Its licences, and the detail of each source with the passages read, are in the <a href={REPO} rel="noopener">source code</a>.</p>

<h2 id="site">This website</h2>
<p>Illustrations: Traces Blanches.</p>
